  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nThrough the middle of the upcoming work week, following the \ndeparture of this dynamic weekend system, we can expect dry \nconditions, and transient upper level ridging, resulting in \ntemperatures slowly warming closer to seasonal levels (despite \ndaytime highs likely remaining a few degrees below the daily \nnormals). By late week, ensembles diverge with respect to another\ndisturbance possibly moving through the area, but guidance seem\nto be trending toward a relatively weak transient upper \nlow/positively tilted shortwave that is then followed by more\nridging by the end of next weekend. Regardless of the outcome, \nfairly benign conditions seem to be the most likely outcome. The \ntrajectory of the late week system is not favorable for rain \nchances, with its residence time too short for better quality \nmoisture to be pulled into the area, and if it remains an open \nwave, its positive tilt does not bode well for providing upper \nlevel support for precipitation. NBM PoPs with the latest forecast\nhave fallen to 10% or less Friday into Saturday.",
